// EXPECT: E0223 — `~` is a bitwise complement, not a boolean one (ADR-0042 §4)
// `!` is the boolean negation. A `bool` is one byte and its complement is 254, which is not
// a `bool` at all — so the help line names `!` rather than leaving the reader to guess.
main :: () {
    a := true;
    b := ~a;
}
